 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance approving Amendment No. 1 to the Memorandum of Agreement (“MOA”) by and between The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, acting by and through the Nashville Fire Department (“NFD”) Emergency Medical Services Division, and Vanderbilt University Medical Center, extending the term of an agreement to provide students with clinical training through the Emergency Medical Technician Externship Program.\n..body\nWHEREAS, pursuant to BL2024-231, an agreement between The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, acting by and through the Nashville Fire Department (“NFD”) Emergency Medical Services Division, and Vanderbilt University Medical Center specified the parties’ benefits and obligations regarding the participation and clinical training of students enrolled in the Emergency Medical Technician Program; and,\nWHEREAS, the parties desire to extend the term of this agreement for an additional three (3) years through December 31, 2029; and,\nWHEREAS, it is to the benefit of the citizens of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County that this amendment be approved.\nNOW, THEREFORE BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.  \tThat Amendment No. 1 to the Memorandum of Agreement by and between The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, acting by and through the Nashville Fire Department (“NFD”) Emergency Medical Services Division and Vanderbilt University Medical Center, providing students with clinical training through the Emergency Medical Technician Externship Program, a copy of which is attached hereto and incorporated herein, is hereby approved.\nSection 2.  \tThat this Ordinance shall take effect from and after its adoption, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n\n"
}
